{
  "category": "Single Horn Pokémon",
  "entries": [
    {
      "text": "This powerful POKéMON thrusts its prized horn under its enemies’ bellies then lifts and throws them.",
      "version": "gold"
    },
    {
      "text": "Usually docile, but if disturbed while sipping honey, it chases off the intruder with its horn.",
      "version": "silver"
    },
    {
      "text": "With its Herculean powers, it can easily throw arou nd an object that is 100 times its own weight.",
      "version": "crystal"
    },
    {
      "text": "HERACROSS charges in a straight line at its foe, slips beneath the foe’s grasp, and then scoops up and hurls the opponent with its mighty horn. This POKéMON even has enough power to topple a massive tree.",
      "version": "ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "HERACROSS has sharp claws on its feet. These are planted firmly into the ground or the bark of a tree, giving the POKéMON a secure and solid footing to forcefully fling away foes with its proud horn.",
      "version": "sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "They gather in forests seeking the sweet sap of trees. It is completely clad in a steel-hard shell. It is proud of its horn, which it uses to fling foes.",
      "version": "emerald"
    },
    {
      "text": "Usually docile, but if disturbed while sipping honey, it chases off the intruder with its horn.",
      "version": "firered"
    },
    {
      "text": "This powerful POKéMON thrusts its prized horn under its enemies’ bellies, then lifts and throws them.",
      "version": "leafgreen"
    },
    {
      "text": "It gathers in forests to search for tree sap, its favorite food. It’s strong enough to hurl foes.",
      "version": "diamond"
    },
    {
      "text": "With powerful legs and claws, it generates enough power to hurl foes over great distances.",
      "version": "pearl"
    },
    {
      "text": "It loves sweet honey. To keep all the honey to itself, it hurls rivals away with its prized horn.",
      "version": "platinum"
    },
    {
      "text": "This powerful Pokémon thrusts its prized horn under its enemies’ bellies, then lifts and throws them.",
      "version": "heartgold"
    },
    {
      "text": "It is usually docile, but if it is disturbed while sipping honey, it chases off the intruder with its horn.",
      "version": "soulsilver"
    },
    {
      "text": "It loves sweet honey. To keep all the honey to itself, it hurls rivals away with its prized horn.",
      "version": "black"
    },
    {
      "text": "It loves sweet honey. To keep all the honey to itself, it hurls rivals away with its prized horn.",
      "version": "white"
    },
    {
      "text": "No matter how heavy its opponents, it flings them far away with its prized horn.",
      "version": "black-2"
    },
    {
      "text": "No matter how heavy its opponents, it flings them far away with its prized horn.",
      "version": "white-2"
    },
    {
      "text": "This powerful Pokémon thrusts its prized horn under its enemies’ bellies, then lifts and throws them.",
      "version": "x"
    },
    {
      "text": "With its Herculean powers, it can easily throw around an object that is 100 times its own weight.",
      "version": "y"
    },
    {
      "text": "Heracross charges in a straight line at its foe, slips beneath the foe’s grasp, and then scoops up and hurls the opponent with its mighty horn. This Pokémon even has enough power to topple a massive tree.",
      "version": "omega-ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "Heracross has sharp claws on its feet. These are planted firmly into the ground or the bark of a tree, giving the Pokémon a secure and solid footing to forcefully fling away foes with its proud horn.",
      "version": "alpha-sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "It’s proud of its thick horn. In Alola, its biggest rival is Vikavolt, which it’s always fighting with.",
      "version": "ultra-sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "It roams through forests searching for sweet nectar. Although it boasts fantastic physical strength, it’s not that good at flying.",
      "version": "ultra-moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "Heracross loves sweet sap and will go looking through forests for it. The Pokémon uses its two antennae to pick up scents as it searches.",
      "version": "sword"
    },
    {
      "text": "This Pokémon takes pride in its strength, which allows it to lift things 100 times heavier than itself with no trouble at all.",
      "version": "shield"
    },
    {
      "text": "This Pokémon has an unparalleled horn. Heracross itself demonstrates tremendous power—it's capable of throwing several people trained in the traditional arts of war at once.",
      "version": "legends-arceus"
    }
  ],
